1
00:00:01,067 --> 00:00:01,767
<i>Your husband and I are not
in a relationship.</i>

2
00:00:01,900 --> 00:00:03,000
<i> I hope you can forgive me.</i>

3
00:00:03,133 --> 00:00:04,767
<i> Sorry if I doubted you.</i>

4
00:00:04,900 --> 00:00:06,633
<i> I'm also at fault.</i>

5
00:00:06,767 --> 00:00:09,733
<i>Does this mean that our family
is okay again?</i>

6
00:00:09,867 --> 00:00:10,733
<i> Are we whole again?</i>

7
00:00:10,867 --> 00:00:12,133
<i> We are not broken.</i>

8
00:00:12,267 --> 00:00:14,667
<i>Here in my heart,
our family is whole.</i>

9
00:00:14,800 --> 00:00:18,133
<i>My contact said that Golda
has already given a statement.</i>

10
00:00:18,267 --> 00:00:20,000
<i> Matias, you know the drill.</i>

11
00:00:20,133 --> 00:00:21,500
<i> Joey is texting.</i>

12
00:00:21,633 --> 00:00:22,667
<i> Emergency?</i>

13
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:24,700
<i>We need volunteers
for the games.</i>

14
00:00:24,833 --> 00:00:27,200
<i>Hey, why are you here?
Are you a stalker?</i>

15
00:00:27,333 --> 00:00:30,100
<i>This is my sister's foundation.
What are you guys doing here?</i>

16
00:00:30,233 --> 00:00:31,633
<i>We are participating
in the games.</i>

17
00:00:31,767 --> 00:00:36,800
<i>Welcome to our foundation's
annual "Palarong Puso"!</i>

18
00:00:36,967 --> 00:00:41,300
<i> Let the games begin!</i>

19
00:00:41,433 --> 00:00:43,033
<i> That's how you want to play?</i>

20
00:00:43,167 --> 00:00:45,167
<i>- It was an accident.
- Okay, go.</i>

21
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:46,567
<i> You think I don't know?</i>

22
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:47,867
<i>You two are doing it
intentionally.</i>

23
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:49,933
<i>I didn't mean it.
If it was intentional.</i>

24
00:00:50,067 --> 00:00:51,533
<i> I would've done this.</i>

25
00:00:51,667 --> 00:00:53,333
<i> You cannot do that, Jin Ho.</i>

26
00:00:53,467 --> 00:00:55,200
<i> Can you just stop fighting?</i>

27
00:00:55,333 --> 00:00:56,167
<i> You're on your own.</i>

28
00:00:56,300 --> 00:00:57,233
<i> Now I get it.</i>

29
00:00:57,367 --> 00:01:00,267
<i>I understand why you like Joey
so much.</i>

30
00:01:00,400 --> 00:01:01,900
<i> They like you.</i>

31
00:01:02,033 --> 00:01:04,467
<i>Hey, that's impossible.
I'm pretty to the max.</i>

32
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:05,533
<i> That's true.</i>

33
00:01:05,667 --> 00:01:10,267
<i>Our next game is the longest
line!</i>

34
00:01:10,433 --> 00:01:12,400
<i> So on the count of three...</i>

35
00:01:12,533 --> 00:01:16,400
<i> One, two, three, go!</i>

36
00:01:40,767 --> 00:01:43,133
Hey, stop that, stop that.
That's not allowed.

37
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:47,567
Hey, that's not allowed.
Go inside. Get dressed.

38
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:50,000
Andrew, come on. Get dressed.

39
00:01:53,167 --> 00:01:55,100
Oh, my God.

40
00:01:55,233 --> 00:01:59,400
Get dressed, get dressed.

41
00:01:59,533 --> 00:02:03,000
Oh, come on, hurry up!
Hurry up! Get dressed!

42
00:02:03,133 --> 00:02:05,033
- My God!
- We won.

43
00:02:05,167 --> 00:02:06,067
Wait a minute.

44
00:02:06,200 --> 00:02:09,667
It's a tie between Team Andrew,
Peter, and...

45
00:02:11,933 --> 00:02:13,967
Hey here.

46
00:02:14,100 --> 00:02:16,933
Cool down first so you don't
undress there.

47
00:02:18,067 --> 00:02:19,533
Come on, it's heavy.

48
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:23,033
Thank you.

49
00:02:23,167 --> 00:02:24,067
Sorry.

50
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:27,200
We promised them
that we would do our best.

51
00:02:27,333 --> 00:02:29,733
We too, fight if we fight.
Right, Jin Ho?

52
00:02:29,867 --> 00:02:30,833
For sure!

53
00:02:30,967 --> 00:02:33,200
That's how it should be
and not be sore losers

54
00:02:33,333 --> 00:02:35,733
and take off your clothes.
It's embarrassing for the kids.

55
00:02:35,867 --> 00:02:36,933
You're driving us crazy.

56
00:02:38,200 --> 00:02:41,333
Joey, I have a question.

57
00:02:41,467 --> 00:02:45,400
So among the three of us,
who's the best body?

58
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:50,667
I was just looking at the game,
not at you. You smell.

59
00:02:50,833 --> 00:02:52,567
Okay, okay.
You want us to show again?

60
00:02:52,700 --> 00:02:57,067
Oh, no! I don't want to see.
Yuck. Stop right there.

61
00:02:57,200 --> 00:02:58,633
You know, the next game
is about to start.

62
00:02:58,767 --> 00:03:00,533
Hurry up there.

63
00:03:00,667 --> 00:03:04,000
You smell! Don't be like that.
Hey, let's go, quick.

64
00:03:04,133 --> 00:03:08,667
I think she's just shy because
she thinks I have the best body.

65
00:03:12,367 --> 00:03:14,567
- Show. Show it.
- Here, here.

66
00:03:14,700 --> 00:03:16,567
Is that what you two
are showing?

67
00:03:16,700 --> 00:03:19,000
That's nothing compared to this.

68
00:03:20,133 --> 00:03:21,567
That's not impressive either.

69
00:03:21,733 --> 00:03:22,933
Go home now.

70
00:03:24,433 --> 00:03:26,767
You're arrogant. Let's go.

71
00:03:26,900 --> 00:03:29,200
Grumpy.

72
00:03:29,333 --> 00:03:32,133
Did everyone enjoy it?

73
00:03:36,333 --> 00:03:39,633
You know, we enjoyed it too,
because they're really good,

74
00:03:39,767 --> 00:03:41,667
especially in the Pie Eating
Contest!

75
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:44,067
My favorite, Friend,
was the relay.

76
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:45,967
Didn't they do well in that?

77
00:03:46,100 --> 00:03:49,267
Yes. That means,
you all are great!

78
00:03:49,400 --> 00:03:51,267
And as early as now,

79
00:03:51,400 --> 00:03:55,767
I congratulate you all
because you did your best.

80
00:03:55,933 --> 00:03:59,733
And for me, you are all winners!

81
00:04:02,433 --> 00:04:04,300
But of course, this is it.

82
00:04:04,433 --> 00:04:08,500
You are the top 4 teams,
as I said earlier,

83
00:04:08,633 --> 00:04:12,167
who will meet to play tug
of war.

84
00:04:12,300 --> 00:04:17,000
So it's like this: Two teams
will fight, right?

85
00:04:17,133 --> 00:04:20,200
Yes, and whoever wins
against you,

86
00:04:20,333 --> 00:04:23,533
they will be the ones
to face off in the final round.

87
00:04:23,667 --> 00:04:24,967
- There.
- Yes!

88
00:04:25,100 --> 00:04:27,967
So now, we'll call out
the names.

89
00:04:28,133 --> 00:04:32,433
Okay, let's go with the ladies
first. Joey and Mary.

90
00:04:32,567 --> 00:04:37,233
Of course, Peter and Lito, too.

91
00:04:37,367 --> 00:04:41,467
Yes, come here too,
Jin Ho and Nono.

92
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:42,333
Yes!

93
00:04:42,467 --> 00:04:44,767
And Andrew and Jeff.

94
00:04:44,900 --> 00:04:46,900
That's it!

95
00:04:49,533 --> 00:04:50,967
So, I have a question.

96
00:04:51,100 --> 00:04:51,700
Yes?

97
00:04:51,833 --> 00:04:53,833
Whose team will go together?

98
00:04:53,967 --> 00:04:55,800
That's a very good question.

99
00:04:55,933 --> 00:05:01,467
But of course, since they are
the only girls in this game,

100
00:05:01,633 --> 00:05:04,400
they will pick the,
you know, yeah,

101
00:05:04,533 --> 00:05:06,333
the team that they will partner
with, okay?

102
00:05:06,467 --> 00:05:08,100
- Okay, that's it?
- Okay. Do you understand?

103
00:05:08,233 --> 00:05:10,433
- Understand!
- Perfect. Go!

104
00:05:14,700 --> 00:05:18,767
- Team Andrew!
- Yes!

105
00:05:29,700 --> 00:05:31,400
We can handle those!

106
00:05:32,533 --> 00:05:35,133
Stay focused! Fighting!

107
00:05:35,300 --> 00:05:37,033
- Are you ready?
- Of course!

108
00:05:37,167 --> 00:05:39,200
- Are you ready?
- Ready!

109
00:05:39,333 --> 00:05:40,233
Okay, game!

110
00:05:40,367 --> 00:05:44,000
Because you are ready,
on the count of three...

111
00:05:44,133 --> 00:05:49,000
One, two, three, pull!

112
00:05:53,200 --> 00:05:54,767
- Did you eat?
- Let's go! Pull!

113
00:05:54,900 --> 00:05:57,667
One, two, pull!

114
00:06:01,567 --> 00:06:03,400
We won!

115
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:07,467
- Let's go!
- We have a winner!

116
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:09,667
<i> Congratulations, guys!</i>

117
00:06:13,467 --> 00:06:14,833
Sorry, sorry.

118
00:06:14,967 --> 00:06:16,633
Sorry too.

119
00:06:16,767 --> 00:06:17,733
Are you okay?

120
00:06:24,900 --> 00:06:25,800
Oh no, come on.

121
00:06:26,933 --> 00:06:27,633
What happened?

122
00:06:27,767 --> 00:06:29,333
You're bleeding.

123
00:06:29,467 --> 00:06:31,533
Come on, rest for now, Mary.

124
00:06:31,667 --> 00:06:32,800
Thank you.

125
00:06:37,167 --> 00:06:40,900
I told you not to hurt anyone,
didn't I?

126
00:06:41,067 --> 00:06:42,967
You know, because you were
such an attention seeker,

127
00:06:43,100 --> 00:06:45,967
and you were so competitive,
the kid got hurt.

128
00:06:47,700 --> 00:06:50,100
I'm sorry, Joey,
we didn't mean to.

129
00:06:50,233 --> 00:06:54,000
You know, I brought you here
because I wanted to thank you.

130
00:06:54,133 --> 00:06:56,567
Do you know this is
a children's game?

131
00:06:56,700 --> 00:06:59,033
But it seems like you're
the childish ones.

132
00:07:00,567 --> 00:07:04,767
You know, this happened,
it's all part of the game.

133
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:08,733
It's not part of the game
when you throw eggs.

134
00:07:08,867 --> 00:07:10,433
Childish.

135
00:07:24,467 --> 00:07:29,267
Just stay here, driver,
and someone will help me.

136
00:07:31,600 --> 00:07:35,300
I'll help you too,
so we can be quick.

137
00:07:36,433 --> 00:07:37,267
There.

138
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:38,833
Thank you.

139
00:07:38,967 --> 00:07:40,067
Thank you too.

140
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:41,467
Be careful.

141
00:07:52,233 --> 00:07:53,867
How do I...

142
00:07:58,867 --> 00:08:02,300
We need to her that before
she goes inside.

143
00:08:08,500 --> 00:08:09,300
Mother.

144
00:08:09,433 --> 00:08:11,000
Hey, Joey.

145
00:08:11,133 --> 00:08:13,867
- Help! Please help.
- Let me help you.

146
00:08:15,100 --> 00:08:17,100
I thought...

147
00:08:17,233 --> 00:08:20,167
You're still busy inside,
that's why you're not answering.

148
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:23,933
Earlier, you were a bit busy,
but the game is over.

149
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:25,267
Let me help you.

150
00:08:25,400 --> 00:08:26,733
Just a moment, Joey.

151
00:08:27,900 --> 00:08:29,367
Are you okay?

152
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:34,033
When you're lucky, the mother
and daughter are together.

153
00:08:34,167 --> 00:08:35,867
I'm okay.

154
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,467
Why do you look like that?

155
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:40,933
Your face looks long.

156
00:08:41,067 --> 00:08:42,333
No, no, Mother.

157
00:08:42,467 --> 00:08:44,767
It's obvious, Joey.

158
00:08:44,900 --> 00:08:46,500
What is it?

159
00:08:46,633 --> 00:08:50,733
Maybe Delgado will get
the message.

160
00:08:50,867 --> 00:08:53,867
He'll just shut up
and keep quiet in jail.

161
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,633
Won't he even go crazier, Boss?

162
00:08:56,800 --> 00:08:58,867
Let him go crazy...

163
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:01,233
if he wants to never see
his family again.

164
00:09:01,367 --> 00:09:03,133
Let's work out a strategy
for this.

165
00:09:12,300 --> 00:09:16,967
Jin Ho and Peter
are so competitive,

166
00:09:17,100 --> 00:09:21,167
to the point that a kid got hurt
because of them.

167
00:09:21,300 --> 00:09:23,400
Oh my, what happened to the kid?

168
00:09:23,533 --> 00:09:26,600
She just got a scratch,
but she's been treated.

169
00:09:26,733 --> 00:09:28,867
Those two are just really
annoying.

170
00:09:29,033 --> 00:09:31,400
Joey, you're a bit OA too.

171
00:09:31,533 --> 00:09:33,700
I wondered what happened
to the kid.

172
00:09:33,833 --> 00:09:35,133
It turned out it was just
a scratch.

173
00:09:35,267 --> 00:09:36,833
Luckily, she's okay.

174
00:09:36,967 --> 00:09:41,800
My goal today is for you
to enjoy to the fullest.

175
00:09:44,333 --> 00:09:45,767
Oh, come on.

176
00:09:45,900 --> 00:09:48,300
Mother, let me. I'll help you.

177
00:09:50,933 --> 00:09:52,500
There, someone will help.

178
00:09:52,633 --> 00:09:53,633
That's right.

179
00:09:53,767 --> 00:09:55,033
Two guys have arrived, Boss.

180
00:09:55,167 --> 00:09:57,300
Those guys don't stand a chance
with us.

181
00:09:57,433 --> 00:09:59,933
If they fight back,
we'll knock them down.

182
00:10:00,067 --> 00:10:02,367
Help, please.
You guys are so big.

183
00:10:02,533 --> 00:10:05,100
Joey, we're really sorry.

184
00:10:05,233 --> 00:10:06,967
You're sorry.

185
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:09,733
We ruined your day.

186
00:10:09,867 --> 00:10:10,900
Peace.

187
00:10:21,367 --> 00:10:22,633
Let's go.

188
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:26,333
Why, Boss?

189
00:10:26,467 --> 00:10:28,133
I thought we could handle those?

190
00:10:28,267 --> 00:10:29,467
Stupid!

191
00:10:29,600 --> 00:10:31,567
The other guy is Berdugo's
brother-in-law.

192
00:10:31,700 --> 00:10:33,333
He can't see me.

193
00:10:33,467 --> 00:10:35,433
You can give him.

194
00:10:35,600 --> 00:10:37,200
- It's okay.
- You can handle that.

195
00:10:43,300 --> 00:10:44,300
What's that?

196
00:10:46,767 --> 00:10:48,400
Let's go.

197
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:50,233
- Hey!
- Oh my...

198
00:10:52,967 --> 00:10:55,400
- Who's there?
- Jin Ho.

199
00:10:58,900 --> 00:11:00,800
- Don't follow...
- Give me that.

200
00:11:03,300 --> 00:11:04,400
Let's go.

201
00:11:04,533 --> 00:11:07,667
Hey, come back here!
You don't know who that is!

202
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:16,400
They are gone.

203
00:11:16,533 --> 00:11:19,133
The other one is crazy.
I saw the other one has a gun.

204
00:11:19,267 --> 00:11:21,767
Both of them have guns.

205
00:11:21,900 --> 00:11:23,400
Did anyone see their faces?

206
00:11:23,533 --> 00:11:24,433
Not me.

207
00:11:24,567 --> 00:11:26,200
Maybe you can use your
intelligence powers

208
00:11:26,333 --> 00:11:28,200
to figure out who they are.

209
00:11:28,333 --> 00:11:30,867
There was no plate on the car.

210
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:33,100
I can't make a trace on them.

211
00:11:34,400 --> 00:11:36,300
What are they planning?

212
00:11:39,233 --> 00:11:41,300
Joey and Ms. Clarissa...

213
00:11:41,467 --> 00:11:44,267
- Let's go, let's go.
- Let's go, let's go.

214
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:47,000
I've already reported
the two-armed men.

215
00:11:47,133 --> 00:11:48,567
They said they'll be doing
the rounds

216
00:11:48,700 --> 00:11:50,733
because there might be someone
else lurking around.

217
00:11:50,867 --> 00:11:54,567
Well, for sure,
they won't come back.

218
00:11:54,700 --> 00:11:58,267
Maybe they're scared of these
troublemakers.

219
00:11:58,400 --> 00:11:59,933
But in fairness,

220
00:12:00,067 --> 00:12:01,900
even if these three are
troublemakers,

221
00:12:02,033 --> 00:12:04,600
they are strong and alert.

222
00:12:04,733 --> 00:12:07,967
They protected me and my mother.

223
00:12:08,100 --> 00:12:09,700
So, thank you.

224
00:12:11,133 --> 00:12:14,200
Well, you guys have probably
saved the day.

225
00:12:14,333 --> 00:12:15,800
But you shouldn't have chased
them anymore.

226
00:12:15,967 --> 00:12:17,600
You saw them with guns.

227
00:12:18,800 --> 00:12:22,667
Maybe those are just carjackers?

228
00:12:22,800 --> 00:12:24,000
Maybe.

229
00:12:24,133 --> 00:12:26,100
That's why they're the ones
in the car.

230
00:12:26,233 --> 00:12:29,000
But why did they bring out
their guns right away

231
00:12:29,133 --> 00:12:31,333
if the car is what they're
after?

232
00:12:33,700 --> 00:12:38,100
Could it be that my daughter
and I are their targets?

233
00:12:39,433 --> 00:12:40,967
Maybe...

234
00:12:41,100 --> 00:12:43,633
maybe this is related to...

235
00:12:43,767 --> 00:12:46,233
My husband's case.

236
00:12:46,367 --> 00:12:48,533
Oh my god, Clarissa.

237
00:12:48,700 --> 00:12:50,500
What if you're right?

238
00:12:50,633 --> 00:12:53,000
Maybe you need security.

239
00:12:54,467 --> 00:12:58,467
Ma'am, we'll just request
it from Chief Lansang.

240
00:12:58,600 --> 00:12:59,600
Maybe, Mother,

241
00:12:59,733 --> 00:13:02,533
the one who framed Father
is really scared too.

242
00:13:02,667 --> 00:13:05,267
Because Father's case
is very strong.

243
00:13:05,400 --> 00:13:08,200
And I'm sure that when Father
is acquitted,

244
00:13:08,333 --> 00:13:10,900
he'll find a way to expose
that syndicate.

245
00:13:12,167 --> 00:13:13,100
When that happens,

246
00:13:13,233 --> 00:13:15,367
our lives will be back
to normal.

247
00:13:15,500 --> 00:13:18,600
We won't be afraid and hide
anymore, right, Mother?

248
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:24,733
Well, you really inherited
that from your father, Joey.

249
00:13:24,867 --> 00:13:27,000
Always positive thinking.

250
00:13:27,133 --> 00:13:29,633
That's why I'm only holding on
to you now.

251
00:13:30,667 --> 00:13:32,300
Of course, Mother.

252
00:13:32,433 --> 00:13:33,933
Never say die?

253
00:13:34,067 --> 00:13:36,633
- Never say die.
- Never say die.

254
00:13:39,267 --> 00:13:40,800
They wanted to join.

255
00:13:40,933 --> 00:13:42,967
You guys got involved.

256
00:13:43,100 --> 00:13:45,767
I was going to have a surprise
for you, Berdugo.

257
00:13:45,900 --> 00:13:49,067
I thought I'd get Delgado's
family.

258
00:13:49,200 --> 00:13:53,067
I was going to scare him
so that the policeman

259
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:57,733
who's a thorn in our throats
would shut up, but I failed.

260
00:13:57,900 --> 00:13:58,867
<i> Why?</i>

261
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:01,133
Your brother-in-law came.

262
00:14:01,267 --> 00:14:02,933
He even chased us.

263
00:14:03,067 --> 00:14:04,400
<i> Son of a...</i>

264
00:14:04,533 --> 00:14:05,633
<i> Did they see you?</i>

265
00:14:05,767 --> 00:14:06,967
No, Berdugo.

266
00:14:07,100 --> 00:14:08,533
It was dark.

267
00:14:08,667 --> 00:14:10,733
They didn't catch us.

268
00:14:10,867 --> 00:14:13,900
<i>This problem with Delgado
has been going on for too long.</i>

269
00:14:14,033 --> 00:14:16,867
<i>We need to bring out
all the aces.</i>

270
00:14:19,167 --> 00:14:22,100
For our 4th place,
the winner is the team of...

271
00:14:22,233 --> 00:14:24,767
That's Team Joey!

272
00:14:27,300 --> 00:14:28,433
There!

273
00:14:28,600 --> 00:14:30,967
- Congratulations!
- Yes!

274
00:14:31,100 --> 00:14:35,433
Next up, our 3rd place,
is the team of...

275
00:14:35,833 --> 00:14:38,467
Andrew! Team, Andrew!

276
00:14:41,633 --> 00:14:45,467
The 2nd place is the team of...

277
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:51,333
- Yes, Team Peter!
- Peter!

278
00:14:51,467 --> 00:14:52,867
- Congratulations!
- Congrats!

279
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:56,967
That means, our champion
is the team of...

280
00:14:57,100 --> 00:15:00,000
Team Jin Ho!

281
00:15:04,033 --> 00:15:07,533
Congratulations, winners!

282
00:15:07,667 --> 00:15:09,933
Congratulations, everyone!

283
00:15:11,767 --> 00:15:13,567
Yes!

284
00:15:13,700 --> 00:15:15,067
Congrats!

285
00:15:16,967 --> 00:15:18,733
Idol!

286
00:15:26,033 --> 00:15:30,267
Okay, let's take photos.
Photo op now.

287
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:33,400
Let's come here.
Let's all take a picture.

288
00:15:33,533 --> 00:15:35,800
In fairness, that suits you.

289
00:15:35,967 --> 00:15:37,600
You guys are like heroes.

290
00:15:37,733 --> 00:15:40,667
Well, you are our heroes,
both for Mother and me.

291
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:42,567
You know, I admit it.

292
00:15:42,700 --> 00:15:45,800
I know I want to win because you
used to be impressed with me.

293
00:15:45,933 --> 00:15:48,667
But now, you seem to be more
impressed with these two.

294
00:15:48,800 --> 00:15:50,100
Oh, no.

295
00:15:50,233 --> 00:15:51,433
I'm impressed with you.

296
00:15:51,567 --> 00:15:53,500
Besides, our friendship
is deeper,

297
00:15:53,633 --> 00:15:55,100
so don't be insecure.

298
00:15:57,800 --> 00:16:00,767
I have to admit.
It's kind of weird for me.

299
00:16:00,900 --> 00:16:02,900
I'm not used to having friends.

300
00:16:03,033 --> 00:16:07,333
I'm more used to competing,
always giving my best or else...

301
00:16:07,467 --> 00:16:08,867
there will be consequences.

302
00:16:09,033 --> 00:16:12,600
You know, friendship shouldn't
be forced.

303
00:16:12,733 --> 00:16:13,767
Besides,

304
00:16:13,900 --> 00:16:16,533
there shouldn't be any
punishment when you can't do it.

305
00:16:16,667 --> 00:16:18,567
And you don't have to prove
anything to me

306
00:16:18,700 --> 00:16:20,967
because you're already
my friend.

307
00:16:21,100 --> 00:16:25,267
As for me, I'm just happy
because we're allies today.

308
00:16:25,400 --> 00:16:29,800
because I'm not used to being on
the same side.

309
00:16:29,933 --> 00:16:32,433
In fairness, you're okay being
on the same side.

310
00:16:32,567 --> 00:16:36,367
Besides, you seem happier
when I'm by your side,

311
00:16:36,500 --> 00:16:38,033
I mean, the three of us.

312
00:16:40,133 --> 00:16:44,067
You know, it's hard to find true
friends these days,

313
00:16:44,233 --> 00:16:48,500
so we should value each other,
not fight.

314
00:16:48,633 --> 00:16:51,867
So we should take care
of our friendship, right?

315
00:16:52,000 --> 00:16:53,800
What? Solid?

316
00:16:53,933 --> 00:16:55,633
Never say die.

317
00:16:55,767 --> 00:16:57,367
Solid.

318
00:16:57,500 --> 00:16:59,167
Game.

319
00:16:59,300 --> 00:17:00,733
You know, let's take a picture
the four of us.

320
00:17:00,867 --> 00:17:01,533
The four of us?

321
00:17:01,667 --> 00:17:03,267
Mister, please take a picture.

322
00:17:03,400 --> 00:17:04,467
Sorry, sorry to you.

323
00:17:04,600 --> 00:17:05,433
Thank you.

324
00:17:05,567 --> 00:17:06,667
You're in the middle now.

325
00:17:10,233 --> 00:17:11,700
Yes! Congrats, Boy!

326
00:17:11,833 --> 00:17:13,933
Hey my ears,
your voice is so loud.

327
00:17:34,967 --> 00:17:36,633
Jin Ho!

328
00:17:36,767 --> 00:17:38,000
Wait!

329
00:17:38,133 --> 00:17:39,167
Joey?

330
00:17:40,367 --> 00:17:41,867
- Yeah.
- Is there a problem?

331
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:44,867
No, no. I just want to give you
something.

332
00:17:48,967 --> 00:17:51,267
I just wanted to give
that to you

333
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:54,733
so that no matter where you go,

334
00:17:54,867 --> 00:17:58,100
you'll never forget that you
have friends, that you have us.

335
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:00,633
Thank you.

336
00:18:00,767 --> 00:18:02,900
Just be careful,
and don't miss us.

337
00:18:03,033 --> 00:18:05,133
Don't miss me.

338
00:18:05,267 --> 00:18:06,833
Bye! Be careful!

339
00:18:06,967 --> 00:18:08,667
Okay, bye.

340
00:18:22,200 --> 00:18:23,633
<i>- Jin Ho!
- Go!</i>

341
00:18:23,767 --> 00:18:25,700
<i>- Joey, come on!
- Get out of here!</i>

342
00:18:25,833 --> 00:18:27,833
<i>Let's go ahead!
Let's leave them!</i>

343
00:18:27,967 --> 00:18:29,533
<i>- Jin Ho!
- Oppa!</i>

344
00:18:29,667 --> 00:18:30,900
<i> We are worried about you!</i>

345
00:18:31,033 --> 00:18:31,933
<i> I'm okay.</i>

346
00:18:32,067 --> 00:18:33,167
<i> You're bleeding.</i>

347
00:18:33,300 --> 00:18:34,467
<i> It's nothing.</i>

348
00:18:34,600 --> 00:18:35,967
<i>No, let's go to the hospital.
You have to get checked.</i>

349
00:18:36,100 --> 00:18:38,933
<i>No, I'm really okay.
Don't worry.</i>

350
00:18:40,833 --> 00:18:44,300
<i>- Shot!
- Shot?</i>

351
00:18:47,133 --> 00:18:48,333
<i> Make it good.</i>

352
00:18:48,467 --> 00:18:52,700
<i> Joey! Come on. Go, Joey.</i>

353
00:18:55,167 --> 00:18:56,933
Theresa...

354
00:18:57,067 --> 00:18:59,367
It's not just about you and me.

355
00:19:01,667 --> 00:19:04,300
I have to protect my friends.

356
00:19:04,433 --> 00:19:05,667
No...

357
00:19:10,467 --> 00:19:12,467
I have to protect Joey.

358
00:19:32,067 --> 00:19:35,467
Judge, can I disturb you
even though you are busy?

359
00:19:35,600 --> 00:19:37,633
Matias, what do you need?

360
00:19:37,767 --> 00:19:39,500
We need to talk.

361
00:19:49,733 --> 00:19:51,300
Wait, wait, wait.

362
00:19:57,300 --> 00:19:58,400
Is it okay?

363
00:19:58,533 --> 00:19:59,667
Delicious!

364
00:19:59,800 --> 00:20:00,867
Really?

365
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:05,633
Yes, look so domesticated,
you're cooking for Andrew.

366
00:20:06,900 --> 00:20:07,600
What do you mean
by domesticated?

367
00:20:07,733 --> 00:20:09,033
You're something else.

368
00:20:09,167 --> 00:20:14,800
Because this is the only way
I can think of to thank him.

369
00:20:14,933 --> 00:20:17,500
Well, why? Aren't you attracted
to him?

370
00:20:17,633 --> 00:20:21,200
He's tall, handsome,
with almond eyes,

371
00:20:21,333 --> 00:20:22,467
and smells good.

372
00:20:22,600 --> 00:20:25,400
Aren't those kinds
of men your type?

373
00:20:25,533 --> 00:20:27,633
I don't look at him.

374
00:20:27,767 --> 00:20:30,700
So you should look at him.

375
00:20:30,833 --> 00:20:32,267
You'll see.

376
00:20:32,400 --> 00:20:34,233
You know, you're stubborn, too?

377
00:20:34,367 --> 00:20:36,633
Yeah, right.

378
00:20:36,800 --> 00:20:38,667
This must be okay.

379
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:41,067
This sinigang is delicious.

380
00:20:41,200 --> 00:20:43,267
Oh, no, that's for Andrew.

381
00:20:43,400 --> 00:20:45,300
That's embarrassing.

382
00:20:45,433 --> 00:20:47,200
Isn't it?

383
00:20:47,333 --> 00:20:48,767
Delicious.

384
00:20:48,900 --> 00:20:50,867
Okay, I'll put that on.

385
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:53,133
It might not be enough for
Andrew.

386
00:20:54,100 --> 00:20:55,233
Andrew.

387
00:20:55,367 --> 00:20:57,867
Why is your face like that?
Is there a problem?

388
00:20:58,000 --> 00:21:00,200
- There is.
- Attorney...

389
00:21:03,333 --> 00:21:05,167
I'm sorry, Miss Delgado.

390
00:21:06,900 --> 00:21:09,767
The court did not accept
the witness statement

391
00:21:09,933 --> 00:21:11,700
due to technicalities.

392
00:21:11,833 --> 00:21:12,833
What?

393
00:21:26,400 --> 00:21:28,700
Guys, my vlogger friend texted.

394
00:21:28,833 --> 00:21:30,900
But now, we need to go
to Bolagos Lake first.

395
00:21:31,033 --> 00:21:33,400
They definitely won't find
anything on those bodies.

396
00:21:33,533 --> 00:21:36,500
If this is traced back to me,
I'll throw you next.

397
00:21:36,633 --> 00:21:37,900
When Berdugo catches me,

398
00:21:38,033 --> 00:21:40,367
that's what I'll definitely
end up with.

399
00:21:40,500 --> 00:21:42,567
Joey, I went home as soon
as I found out.

400
00:21:42,733 --> 00:21:44,300
One of the bodies has been
identified

401
00:21:44,433 --> 00:21:45,567
through dental records.

402
00:21:45,700 --> 00:21:48,800
Is Godfather Diego one
of the bodies found?

403
00:21:48,933 --> 00:21:52,400
I just remembered our employee
asking for help.

404
00:21:52,533 --> 00:21:53,333
Clarissa?

405
00:21:53,467 --> 00:21:55,333
I want to meet her as soon
as possible.
